@startuml
title Purchase Request Workflow — Choreography with Persistent Waiting
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ArrowColor #2d7a5c
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam titleFontColor #163d2e
skinparam titleFontSize 16
skinparam titleFontStyle bold
skinparam sequence {
  ActorBackgroundColor #e8f2ec
  ActorBorderColor #1f5c44
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #e8f2ec
  ParticipantBorderColor #1f5c44
  ParticipantFontColor #163d2e
  LifeLineBorderColor #9eabb7
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #f4f6f8
  DatabaseBackgroundColor #d9ede3
  DatabaseBorderColor #1f5c44
  GroupBackgroundColor #fdf3e0
  GroupBorderColor #c9a227
  GroupFontColor #5a4600
  DividerBackgroundColor #f4f6f8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #fff8e7
  BorderColor #c9a227
  FontColor #5a4600
}
skinparam legend {
  BackgroundColor #f4f6f8
  BorderColor #9eabb7
  FontColor #17212b
}

actor Submitter
actor Approver
participant "HTTP boundary" as HTTP
participant "Request / approval services" as Service
participant "Execution coordinator" as Coordinator
participant "Choreography strategy" as Choreography
participant "Run-scoped EventBus" as EventBus
participant "Advance handler" as Handler
participant "Shared step service" as Step
participant "Unit of work" as UoW
database Database

Submitter -> HTTP : submit purchase request + choreography mode
HTTP -> Service : create submission
Service -> UoW : commit purchase request + run + READY cursor + trace
UoW -> Database : transaction
Database --> UoW : committed
Service -> Coordinator : drive(run identity)
Coordinator -> Choreography : open processing scope
Choreography -> EventBus : subscribe handler(run identity)
Choreography -> EventBus : publish Advance(run, expected version)
EventBus -> Handler : synchronous dispatch

loop while committed cursor remains READY
  Handler -> Step : execute one shared step from persisted state
  Step -> UoW : commit attempt/result + retry/next cursor/terminal + trace
  UoW -> Database : transaction
  Database --> UoW : committed state version
  alt next cursor READY
    Handler -> EventBus : publish Advance(run, new version)
    EventBus -> Handler : synchronous dispatch
  else cursor WAITING or TERMINAL
    Handler --> EventBus : stop current advancement
  end
end

Choreography -> EventBus : unsubscribe handler; clear run scope
Choreography --> Coordinator : waiting or terminal
Coordinator --> Service : projection
Service --> HTTP : current status
HTTP --> Submitter : current result

opt run waits for approval
  note over EventBus,Database : No subscriber while waiting;\ndatabase cursor and work item are authoritative.
  Approver -> HTTP : approve or reject
  HTTP -> Service : idempotent decision command
  Service -> UoW : commit decision + READY cursor + trace
  UoW -> Database : transaction with version/uniqueness checks
  Database --> UoW : committed or controlled conflict
  Service -> Coordinator : drive same run identity
  Coordinator -> Choreography : rebuild processing scope from database
  Choreography -> EventBus : subscribe new handler(run identity)
  Choreography -> EventBus : publish Advance(run, committed version)
  EventBus -> Handler : synchronous dispatch
  Handler -> Step : continue shared steps to waiting or terminal
  Step -> UoW : commit each step before next event
  UoW -> Database : transactions
  Database --> UoW : committed
  Choreography -> EventBus : unsubscribe and clear scope
end

legend
EventBus is a transient trigger, not a durable queue or state store.
No Kafka, broker fallback, global run handler, or waiting subscriber.
Automated acceptance exercises the same run-scoped lifecycle.
endlegend
@enduml
